<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Udai Singh of Marwar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1538–1595</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Mota Raja</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Udai Singh, known as Mota Raja, was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rathore">Rathore</a> ruler of Marwar (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jodhpur">Jodhpur</a>) from 1583 to 1595, restored to his kingdom as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar</a>. His daughter married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jahangir">Prince Salim</a>, the future Jahangir, and was the mother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-jahan">Shah Jahan</a>. His many sons and descendants founded Rathore states such as Kishangarh and Ratlam.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/udai-singh-of-marwar.jpg" alt="Udai Singh of Marwar" width="220" height="261" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Udai_Singh_of_Marwar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
